   "body": "**mac/mac-mbp**: adversarial review round 1, reviewer r1295 (Opus 5.5), author w1237 (Sonnet 5.5).\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, r1295, head 0f0fbbd9)**\n\n**REQUEST CHANGES**\n\n1. **High**, `reader.css:243` (`a.video-card .video-pill`) and `:235` (`button.video`). `.videos` and `.videolinks` are children of the article, not of `div.content` (`TopicHTMLBuilder.swift:130-131`), so `0.85em` was 0.85 × body: 14.45 px at 100 %. `var(--fs-85-content)` gives 12.75 px instead. Scenario: a message with a video at 100 %, whose pill and button shrink by 1.7 px. Fix: use `--fs-85`.\n2. **High**, `reader.css:202` (`b.s1`). The `[code]` header is a `b.s1` inside `table.code` (`HFRBBCodeWriter+Shapes.swift:45`). It was 0.85 × 0.85 × content-em (10.84 px at 100 %) and is now 12.75 px. Fix: a floored `0.7225` variable for `table.code b.s1, table.fixed b.s1`.\n3. **Medium**, `reader.css:235` and `:249` (`button.image-tap`, `.image-link`). `reader.js` also places these inside `.signature`. They were 10.84 px at 100 % and are now 12.75 px. Fix: a signature-specific floored variable.\n4. **Medium**, `ReaderTextFloorWebTests.swift:41-45`. The 100 % / 130 % test probes only the first `b.s1` and no video, code or signature image, so findings 1 to 3 stay green. Fix: probe those elements too, and show the test failing at 100 % on the current CSS.\n5. **Low**, `sub` and `sup` (`MessageContentNormalizer.swift:33`). WebKit's `font-size: smaller` gives about 9.2 px at 70 %. Fix: floor them, or name them out of scope.\n\nHolds:\n- `max()` and `min()` with `var()` match `TextScale.pointSize`.\n- No other stylesheet or inline style sets a size.\n- The bubble and trailer ratios are unchanged at 100 %.\n- Moving the scale test from 70 % to 80 % is sound.\n- No legacy behaviour changes, so no ledger entry is needed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
